# Desktop wiring for x-host-live-control (applied by the wave's DESKTOP-WIRE task)

[host/connection.ts] HOST_METHOD: no row needed (browser-live-control.ts holds the method name itself); HOST_CAPABILITIES.browser is already true.

[host/index.ts] imports, beside `import { type BrowserViewControl, createBrowserView } from './browser-view';`:
  import { type BrowserLiveControl, registerBrowserLiveControlHost } from './browser-live-control';

[host/index.ts] DesktopHostOptions.browser's return type, after `remote: BrowserInputControl['remote'];`:
    /** The streamed page's resize and video limit (`host/browser/liveControl`). */
    liveControl: BrowserLiveControl;

[host/index.ts] createDesktopHost, after `const tabs = createBrowserTabsReporter(connection, () => options.browser().tabs);`:
  registerBrowserLiveControlHost(connection, () => options.browser().liveControl);
The control is resolved per request because the browser is built after the host connection.

[main/index.ts] nothing: createLocalHostRole's `browser` already returns `browserHost.hostRole()`.

NOT A HOT FILE, NOT OWNED BY DESKTOP-WIRE-G1 (the lead decides who applies it): the value comes from
apps/desktop/src/main/browser/host.ts, the only place that holds the remote control (`shown.remote`).
[browser/host.ts] imports, beside the other `import type` lines:
  import type { BrowserLiveControl } from '../host/browser-live-control';
[browser/host.ts] BrowserHost.hostRole()'s return type, after its `remote(method: BrowserRemoteMethod, args: unknown[]): Promise<unknown>;`:
    /** The streamed page's resize and video limit (a phone's resize-request and ready.videoLimit). */
    liveControl: BrowserLiveControl;
[browser/host.ts] createBrowserHost's `hostRole: () => ({ ... })`, after `remote: (method, args) => runBrowserRemoteRequest(browserHost, method, args),`:
      liveControl: { resize: shown.remote.resize, widenVideo: shown.remote.widenVideo },
